-- title:
--   Reducedness of k ⊗_ℤ_{(ℓ)} chartAlgFin in characteristic ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$ not dividing $N$, and let $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ denote the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator (in lowest terms) is coprime to $\ell$. Let $k$ be any field of characteristic $\ell$ equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure; no further hypothesis relating $k$ to $N$ or to the modular function field is imposed, and in particular $k$ is not assumed perfect, algebraically closed or finitely generated. Inside the field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, let $A =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by the single element `jFull N` (the element $j$ of $F$), i.e. the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ in $F$. The assertion is that the commutative ring $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ is reduced: it has no nonzero nilpotent elements.
--
--   This is the geometric reducedness of the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre of the $j$-finite affine chart of the integral model of the modular curve of level $N$, for $\ell \nmid N$, in the classical form going back to Igusa's Kroneckerian model and to Deligne–Rapoport. It is used in the construction of the Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255), where it feeds the proof that the corresponding base change of the chart is integrally closed over a discrete valuation ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_isReduced_chartAlgFin_tensor.lean

